            {
                "entry_id": "73aea07b-d06c-3fc1-869d-52f16033e378",
                "word": "bathmologie",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "204e57f7-83a4-438e-b07e-5f4068162092",
                        "entry_id": "73aea07b-d06c-3fc1-869d-52f16033e378",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "bathmologies"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c75c6be3-7ba3-389c-880e-9379ab7de910",
                        "entry_id": "73aea07b-d06c-3fc1-869d-52f16033e378",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Étude des degrés de signification des mots, des « échelonnements de langage », selon Roland Barthes. Branche de la sémantique. Recherche sur les connotations d’un mot."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Didactique"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b3bbf019-2893-4ea4-b375-d964327b4fc6",
                                "sense_id": "c75c6be3-7ba3-389c-880e-9379ab7de910",
                                "text": "Tout discours est pris dans le jeu des degrés. On peut appeler ce jeu : bathmologie. […] une science nouvelle : celle des échelonnements de langage […] : elle enjambera, comme on saute une marche, toute expression."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "6844e7cc-8c84-38c2-9a3a-89a19428ae83",
                        "entry_id": "73aea07b-d06c-3fc1-869d-52f16033e378",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Jeu sur les différents degrés du discours : ex. second degré, ou (ironique) 36ème degré… ; « science à demi plaisante des niveaux de langage »."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "cf6f2be6-7a46-40a9-84a6-6984a112b758",
                                "sense_id": "6844e7cc-8c84-38c2-9a3a-89a19428ae83",
                                "text": "Il [Renaud Camus] se trouve surtout au cœur de cette science des degrés ou bathmologie souhaitée par Roland Barthes de tous ses vœux et à laquelle Renaud Camus aura donné une expansion et un succès indéniables."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6bfb158f-7f5e-4ec6-9de9-fac18dd17ec3",
                                "sense_id": "6844e7cc-8c84-38c2-9a3a-89a19428ae83",
                                "text": "La bathmologie est la meilleure manière de montrer que deux « oui » peuvent être plus éloignés l’un de l’autre qu’un « oui » et un « non », ce qui, politiquement, aujourd’hui, devrait faire réfléchir nos chers amis les citoyens…"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "46b63de1-6148-41be-9084-7c6386e5f492",
                        "source_entry_id": "73aea07b-d06c-3fc1-869d-52f16033e378",
                        "target_lang_word": "bathmology",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "bathmology",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "51b49e14-d1eb-35fc-a2d9-d761db460f6e",
                                        "entry_id": "a04cd9a6-290b-339e-88bc-6896367236ca",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The science/study of the interplay of \\\"degrees\\\" - or, levels of linguistic self-referentiality - in discourse"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a1d77421-6577-4e9c-94ac-0f8764f49936",
                                                "sense_id": "51b49e14-d1eb-35fc-a2d9-d761db460f6e",
                                                "text": "Every discourse is caught up in the interplay of degrees. We might call this interplay bathmology. A neologism is not superfluous if it gives us the notion of a new science: that of the degrees of language."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2d6ed5c6-4376-4b53-8d5a-1bcb82a0773c",
                                                "sense_id": "51b49e14-d1eb-35fc-a2d9-d761db460f6e",
                                                "text": "The qualitative distances separating love, hate, and indifference are what we could learn from a science of degrees, a “bathmology” like the one Barthes dreamed of for the gradations of language."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2573a8d5-3052-44c0-97a1-4a08a5016935",
                                                "sense_id": "51b49e14-d1eb-35fc-a2d9-d761db460f6e",
                                                "text": "When it addresses itself distinctly to the Young-Girl, the Spectacle is not above a bit of bathmology."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dcd1488b-45d4-4f73-aae6-c78f8a3d0aca",
                                                "sense_id": "51b49e14-d1eb-35fc-a2d9-d761db460f6e",
                                                "text": "While bathmology is not the master key for unlocking the enigma of return, we can think the different positions stake out by the writers in this book as following a trajectory that leads from anti-modernist resumption or rehabilitation (a willful regression that positions itself as a post-critical progression) through 'bathmological' meta-discursive gestures (a critical repetition that changes the meaning of conventions and forms) and finally to spectral poetics which blur the very possibility of defining a clear discursive position or literary self-identity."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ab1e09c4-f9fc-4f8f-8175-63eb63d60ddf",
